### HEADLINE FINDING: China Telecom NR-SA injects TLS RST keyed on SNI ###
  A/B on the SAME device minutes apart:
  - WiFi + hostname 120-79-148-0.sslip.io:8443  -> RUN_END completed, REPORT http=200 (run 019f59ad)
  - Cellular + hostname (sslip.io AND nip.io)    -> Connection reset DURING handshake (RST injection)
  - Cellular + bare IP https://120.79.148.0:8443 -> SSLPeerUnverifiedException (TLS handshake COMPLETED, cert just !match IP)
  => port 8443 + TLS work on cellular; the RST is triggered by SNI hostname content, not the port/host.
  => E-01 forensic/AB/continuity over cellular are BLOCKED by this carrier middlebox; not runnable without SNI workaround.
  ICMP baseline over cellular: ping 120.79.148.0 avg 69ms (23-132), baidu avg 29ms -> host reachable, IP-layer fine.
  Server liveness confirmed independently: device WiFi run REPORT http=200 at 12:13 same session.

